    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d685-a4">

                <pb facs="1116" n="980" sameAs="frus:frus1888p1/pg980"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 4 in No.
                    226.—Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Comte de Sesmaisons to Mr. Reine.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Legation of the French Republic in Hayti</hi>,<lb/><hi
                                rendition="#italic">Cape Hayti</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1888-11-21"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >November</hi> 21, 1888</date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: We have traveled 185 miles to bring
                    propositions of reconciliation as friends of Hayti. We have offered to the
                    gentlemen, members of the committee of Cape Hayti, to come on board the <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Bisson</hi>, neutral territory. Those gentlemen refuse.
                    We can not do more,; we leave them the responsibility of their refusal.</p>
                <p>Receive, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed>
                        <list>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">Comte de Sesmaisons.</hi></item>
                            <item><hi rendition="#small-caps">M. Reine</hi>,</item>
                        </list>
                    </signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
